<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.huffmanwrites.sitrep-watchdog</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/bin/bash</string>
    <string>/Users/prh/Developer/huffmanwrites/scripts/sitrep-watchdog-runner.sh</string>
  </array>
  <!-- Watches for a SITREP edition that does not exist. Every other job alerts
       when it fails; this one alerts when the 06:00 job never ran at all, which
       nothing else can see. Added 2026-10-08 at Philip's request.

       Four times a day, and the first is 07:00 CT: the run starts at 06:00 and
       finished at 06:05:58 on its first unattended morning, so 07:00 leaves
       about an hour for a slow pack plus the Pages deploy. The later three are
       not more chances to notice the same thing — they cover the case where the
       machine was asleep at 07:00 (launchd runs a missed calendar event on
       wake) and the case where an edition was published and then lost. The
       checker alerts once per day per kind, so four checks cannot become four
       banners; the later ones log that the alert was already raised.

       RunAtLoad is on for the machine that was OFF, not asleep: launchd does
       not run a missed StartCalendarInterval event at boot, so without this a
       morning spent powered down would be reported by nothing until 12:00, and
       a login after the deadline is the first honest moment to look. A load
       before 07:00 says nothing at all — the checker exits 0 with "not due
       until 07:00 CT", so a login at 05:00 cannot raise a banner about a report
       whose writer has not started.

       The array form is deliberate and it works: `com.huffmanwrites.docket-watch`
       has carried an array of two dicts since 2026-09-20 and fires at both
       times, every day, with the installed copy matching the repo copy. See the
       note in skills/scheduled-job.md for why the older claim that launchd
       ignores an array was wrong. -->
  <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
  <array>
    <dict>
      <key>Hour</key>
      <integer>7</integer>
      <key>Minute</key>
      <integer>0</integer>
    </dict>
    <dict>
      <key>Hour</key>
      <integer>12</integer>
      <key>Minute</key>
      <integer>0</integer>
    </dict>
    <dict>
      <key>Hour</key>
      <integer>18</integer>
      <key>Minute</key>
      <integer>0</integer>
    </dict>
    <dict>
      <key>Hour</key>
      <integer>22</integer>
      <key>Minute</key>
      <integer>0</integer>
    </dict>
  </array>
  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <true/>
  <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
  <string>/Users/prh/Developer/huffmanwrites</string>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>/Users/prh/Library/Logs/sitrep-watchdog.out.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>/Users/prh/Library/Logs/sitrep-watchdog.err.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
